@startuml BootDiagnostics
!include theme.puml

' File-local: stock PlantUML draws section dividers as a white box, which
' leaves the theme's white text unreadable.
skinparam sequenceDividerBackgroundColor #2F4F4F
skinparam sequenceDividerBorderColor #708090
skinparam sequenceDividerFontColor #ffffff

title Boot Diagnostics - why did the controller restart?\nCaptured at boot, published on connect (added 2026-10-30)

participant "Reset\n(hardware / software)" as Reset
participant "setup()\nmain.cpp" as Setup
participant "NVS\nnamespace: boot" as NVS
participant "Serial\n921600" as Serial
participant "MQTTTask" as MQTTTask
participant "Broker" as Broker
participant "Observer\n(HA, operator)" as Obs

autonumber

== At boot, before any task starts ==

Reset -> Setup : ESP32 starts
Setup -> Setup : nvs_flash_init()
note right of Setup
  The capture sits immediately AFTER this, because it is
  the first point at which Preferences can be opened -
  and before any task exists, so the two globals it fills
  need no mutex.
end note

Setup -> Setup : esp_reset_reason()
Setup -> Setup : 9 static_asserts pin our codes\nto esp_reset_reason_t
note right of Setup
  ESP-IDF renumbering its enum would silently mislabel a
  fault report. The asserts turn that into a build failure.
  The real enum has 16 enumerators, not the 11 one might
  assume - it was read from the framework header, not
  from memory.
end note

Setup -> NVS : begin("boot"), count = count + 1\nput count, put last
NVS --> Setup : boots
Setup -> Serial : BOOT #43 reason=task_wdt (code 6)  <-- ABNORMAL

== Later, on every MQTT connect ==

MQTTTask -> MQTTTask : BootReason::format(buf, 96, code, boots)
MQTTTask -> Broker : publish **retained**\nboiler/status/device/boot
Broker -> Obs : {"reason":"task_wdt","code":6,\n"boots":43,"abnormal":true}
MQTTTask -> Serial : LOG_ERROR if abnormal,\nLOG_INFO otherwise

note over MQTTTask, Obs
  RETAINED, and republished on EVERY connect rather than once.
  The reboot that prompted this facility was noticed hours
  later, and a reconnect must not leave a broker-side gap in
  the only record of it.
end note

note over Reset, Obs
  **WHAT COUNTS AS ABNORMAL** - the classification is the
  whole value of this, so it is deliberate, not a default:

  NOT abnormal: poweron, sw_restart, ext_pin, deepsleep,
  sdio, usb, jtag. sw_restart covers every OTA, every
  cmd/diagnostics reboot and the NVS erase - flagging those
  would make the signal useless in the week you reboot most.
  A power cut is a fact about the house, not a firmware fault.

  ABNORMAL: panic, int_wdt, task_wdt, wdt, brownout, efuse,
  pwr_glitch, cpu_lockup - **and unknown**. An unexplained
  restart is the case this exists for; defaulting it to
  "fine" would reproduce the silence it was added to break.
end note

note over Setup, NVS
  **WHY IT WAS ADDED.** Before 2026-10-30 nothing in the tree
  ever called esp_reset_reason(). A watchdog, a brownout, a
  panic and a commanded reboot were indistinguishable after
  the fact - the device restarted mid-session during that
  night's review and the question simply had no answer.

  It costs more than curiosity: a reboot resets uptime, every
  task's stack high-water mark, and the Modbus error counters.
  Conclusions had twice been drawn from counters that a
  reboot had already cleared.

  CAVEAT, measured on the bench: the counter lives in its own
  boot namespace so a parameter-store wipe does not touch
  it, but boiler/cmd/system nvs_erase erases the WHOLE NVS
  partition and does reset it to 1. The namespace buys less
  protection than it sounds like.

  Source: include/modules/diagnostics/BootReason.h (pure,
  natively tested), capture in main.cpp, publish in
  MQTTTask.cpp. 8 native tests cover the labels, the
  classification, the payload shape, the 96 B worst case and
  the overflow-clears-the-buffer path.
end note

@enduml
